    '3.4':('P3F.1–P3F.2, P3F.16–P3F.56, P3K.6–P3K.38, P3K.40–P3K.41','Eight Mordell–Weil entries and21 configurations in the stated restricted sector enumerated exactly. OS47 has class24. The explicit OS45 family has positive-loop index−3 and class25, a generator; its positive finite covers realize every class in Theta7, with nonproduct mapping tori for nonzero classes. The higher parameter is w_h=exp(−pi i c/(kl)), with c-period2kl and pair(−kl,−4kl) for both sphere signs by the exact signed descent of P3K.33. OS49 topology is proved at all orders3k in the coprime numerator sector, and an exact quadratic norm quotient is constructed. Both OS49 diagonal fans have return class0 at every sphere order3k, both numerator signs and every delta twist, by the actual Cox and joint-cap comparison. P3F.34 corrects the general noncoprime homology: H2 and H3 have the additional Z/g summand, g=gcd(3k,n,3d); the free(9,3,1) example refutes the supplied general-n value. Exhaustive treatment of every construction allowed by Remark8.5 remains under proof. Actual finite-cap, Seifert-base, primitive-fibre and kernel-cancellation restrictions are proved in P3K.15–19, with their source and line data retained. P3F.35 proves integral sphere topology and cap freeness for every one-vertex fan. P3K.20–21 reduce the published root/toric source construction to one simple I1 zero and 26 necessary generic pairs in 16 source profiles; P3K.22 constructs ten primitive-source sphere families and proves their actual line, free quotient, integral topology and positive-loop indices−3,−6,−9,−14. P3K.23 computes the actual fixed-edge flop as A→−5A modulo28, with the signed commutator plumbing and Hopf-clutch comparison retained; the resulting classes are15,2,17,14. P3F.36–40 prove the corrected-line I1star sphere sectors, the two-cap I1star/IV determinant m*n_star+2*n_IV, the reduced-III actual cap, extra smooth-order exclusion on the additive cores, and the exact (Z/m)^2 one-multiplicative-cap obstruction for primitive sources. P3K.24 gives the reduced-III positive return A=−(3l+2), m=4l+3, on both explicit E7 profiles, with the physical closing arrow and signed Thom comparison. P3K.25 proves equality of the K22 returns across every fan retaining the physical delta edge. P3F.41–44 construct and classify the remaining one-cap additive roots and exact affine line lifts. P3F.45 gives the simultaneous primitive-source degree-two obstruction and complete sphere criterion, with every integral gluing degree. P3F.46–47 prove all four IVstar/III pairs and both IIIstar/II pairs, including their exact joint determinant, line norms and all integral maps. P3K.26 supplies the actual signed page, line and return index for sixteen one-cap additive rows, for both norm signs. P3K.27 identifies the primitive-family rotating and Cox normal framings and computes (k,ell)=(-3d,-24) and relative coordinates(6,3d-6,1-d/2). P3F.48 excludes every added smooth or multiplicative effective order above one on all the computed weighted additive cores, including the prime2 case. P3F.49 exhausts the actual OS50 affine source and line lifts by explicit conjugations and transported blowup diagrams. P3K.28 computes all nine joint additive return rows and the two one-I1star source returns A=-2, with both determinant signs and the actual corrected line. P3K.29 gives the exact common-exterior meridian and relative-cycle maps, the full variation after the fixed-edge flop, and integer-zero derivative coordinates on the original nonfixed edges. P3K.30 proves the actual signed rotating and Cox framing comparison for every one- and two-cap page: with H=M*a^2/d it obtains k=-3H, ell=-24*chi and relative coordinates(6*chi,3H-6*chi,chi-H/2), on one positive parameter loop. P3F.50 gives the actual inverse-action comparison for every expanding scalar family, including the unchanged physical fan, cap groups and signed parameter circle. P3F.51 derives the marked generic E7/E6 source equations and carries all root, line, integral-lattice and page maps to every fixed source in the retained profiles. P3F.52 exhausts arbitrary vertical source-line choices by an invariant divisor, its actual root evaluations, finite characters and collar maps. P3K.31 proves the common-exterior stable frame recurrence for every allowed fan and obtains chi*(4-3S)+H*(3*S^2-7)/8, with S=p^2-p*q+q^2 for the physical delta in its actual primitive edge basis. P3K.32 constructs and accounts for all fixed order-one elliptic clutches, including the translated source, retained line divisor, full integral topology, exact closing cochain and page. P3K.33 proves the original and higher single-loop Cox descent for both determinant signs: the pair is (-KL,-4KL), and its all-fan class is KL*(S-1)*(S-3)/8. The original family on the explicit fan v=(3,1), w=(-1,0), delta=v+3*w has class3. No homotopy-sphere class is divided in this descent. P3K.34 proves the component-supported OS49 pair(-6k,-24k) for both norm signs, with the actual mixed-angle and normal-clutch maps; its class on every fan is 3k*(S-1)*(S-3)/4. P3F.53 assembles the exhaustive fixed-source canonical scalar catalogue: sixteen profiles, twenty-six source pairs, thirty-one root branches, thirty nonempty and one determinant exclusion. All 437 exact crosschecks pass, with both regular order-one norm slots retained. P3K.35 constructs the shorter weighted scalar family w=r^b, lambda=w^(M/b), from a literal meromorphic +G lift, every finite-cap commutator, the rational root and cyclic scalar correction. Its individual pair(-3H/b,-24*chi/b), index A/b and all-fan recurrence follow from the actual closed product and integer characteristic naturality; all thirty catalogue branch integrality checks pass. P3F.54 gives the exact E7 marked-node parameter and selected-cusp Tate/Cartier reflection (Z,V,qT) to (qT/Z,V,qT). No one-vertex unimodular fan is preserved by that marked one-turn transport; the actual twofold source cover closes every chart. P3F.55–56 now compute its actual relative smooth return on the specified vertical-edge fan, including the full circle-line, normal-frame and source-collar comparison. P3K.36 proves that the specified Liu–Rollenske construction does not close through one turn of its literal scalar u: the intrinsic Albanese curve of its unique multiple fibre changes from q to -q and has a different j invariant. The actual corrected family has u=w^2, pair(-3,-12), zero reference-fan index and class 3*(S-1)*(S-3)/8 on an arbitrary allowed fan. The printed fixed-a punctured-u construction therefore needs this parameter correction. P3K.37 constructs the component-supported OS49 shorter scalar loop lambda=w^k, with pair(-2k,-8k), relative coordinates(2k,0,0), and all-fan class k*(S-1)*(S-3)/4. As the order and fan vary its exact range consists of every even class modulo28. P3K.38 proves intrinsic minimality of the scalar cover: for all thirty canonical fixed-source branches every biholomorphic endpoint winding is a multiple of M/b, and this bound is attained; for the component-supported OS49 branch the minimum is k. The proof retains the full good-cap and reduced-cap Albanese lattices and applies to arbitrary endpoint biholomorphisms. P3F.55 computes the exact lifted link of (s,rho) mapped to (s^2-rho^2,s*(s^2-rho^2),rho): its double-link linking is1, the required tangent push has Ekholm invariant2, and the literal Whitehead-to-Stiefel arrow gives coefficient1/2. Its Haefliger invariant is1. A nonzero punctured-Kummer test identifies the two published invariant normalizations with every sign fixed. P3F.56 carries the actual closed twofold E7 source family to that link through an embedded trace, the actual Hopf circle line, an explicitly capped S4 correction, and both boundary orientation reversals. On the standard vertical-edge fan, both one-cap E7 sectors have positive source-loop class1, a nonproduct sphere mapping torus, and an obstruction to smooth descent through the degree-two source cover. The remaining source puncture v=0 is being attacked by its marked simultaneous small resolution, the normalization blowup, exact Cartier-line specialization and source-Hom winding. P3K.40 computes the actual first fixed-edge flop of the selected-cusp source loop as class23 modulo28. Its proof retains the sixth Tate winding and an unrestricted four-weight Cox action, verifies the exact quaternionic common-boundary arrow, and uses the actual Hopf quotient to obtain the relative coefficient n=-6 without assigning the still unevaluated other coefficient. P3K.41 proves that, for the stated fixed-source marked affine cap-data scope, fixed-scalar loops have zero return and every varying-scalar loop has winding divisible by M/b, with return equal to the corresponding integer power of K35's shortest scalar return on the same fan. The proof constructs the actual root Lie sheaf, the full orbifold-groupoid Cech comparison, local line-cover lifts through the reduced fibres, the global rational valuation equation and the inverse physical closing arrow; finite torsion kernels remain present until the global calculation removes them. The actual source-suspension transport across the v=0 component flop is still under proof. Its exact residual contraction prevents identifying omitted-origin labels with ordinary CP3 links without the full periodic quotient. The two relative source-loop characteristic integers, later fan transports, moving source/logarithmic sites, component-supported OS49 cap loops and additional unmarked endpoint symmetries remain under their stated scope checks; no uncomputed loop is assigned a class.'),
